# The simple loop reference from plan/00-foundation/01-vision-and-scope.md.
#
# LOAD is what makes the ring solvable: a closed circuit whose duties do not sum to zero has no steady
# state, however square its count (FS2203). HE1's `in=20` is then the circuit's enthalpy datum, which
# a closed circuit's own energy relations cannot supply -- they fix every difference and no absolute
# value (D-65).
#
# `dn` is stated on P1 because nothing chooses a size yet. P3.5's catalogue turns a designation into a
# bore -- it does not pick the designation, which is sizing. Remove it when P3.7 lands: 01's block is
# the canonical form and does not carry it.

fluidscript 1
circuit simpleLoop
fluid water

HE1  heat_exchanger power=30 in=20 out=50
LOAD heat_exchanger power=-30
CV1  valve
PU1  pump
P1   pipe length=25 dn=25

connections
N1 - PU1 - N2 - HE1 - N3 - LOAD - N4 - CV1 - N5 - P1 - N1
